# Kafi — Localization & Constants

## UI text (never hardcode in widgets)

- **Flutter:** All user-visible strings go in `kafi_app/lib/l10n/` — keys in `app_strings.dart`, copy in `locales/en_us.dart` (and `ar_ae.dart` when RTL is enabled).
- **In UI:** use GetX — `AppStrings.someKey.tr` (not raw `'Hello'` in `Text()`).
- **Snackbar/dialog titles:** same rule — use `.tr` keys.
- **Admin (React):** use `admin-panel/src/locales/en.ts` (and `ar.ts` later); import via a small `t()` helper — no literal UI strings in JSX.

```dart
// ❌ BAD — widget
Text('Get Started')

// ✅ GOOD
Text(AppStrings.welcomeGetStarted.tr)
```

Add new keys to **all** locale files when adding a key (at minimum `en_us`; stub `ar_ae` with English until translated).

## Non-UI constants (controllers, services, config)

- Put in `kafi_app/lib/utils/constants/` — one file per domain (`app_constants.dart`, `auth_constants.dart`, `subscription_constants.dart`, etc.).
- **Do not** put user-facing copy in `utils/constants/` — that belongs in l10n.
- **Do not** put magic numbers/strings in controllers (OTP length, free contact limit, plan IDs, mock OTP, route names stay in `config/routes.dart` or constants).

```dart
// ❌ BAD — controller
if (otp.length < 4) ...
Get.snackbar('Error', 'Invalid OTP');

// ✅ GOOD
if (otp.length < AuthConstants.otpLength) ...
Get.snackbar(AppStrings.errorTitle.tr, AppStrings.authInvalidOtp.tr);
```

## GetX controllers

- Import `app_strings.dart` + use `.tr` for any message shown to the user.
- Import domain constants from `utils/constants/` for limits, durations, IDs, feature flags.
- Expose `Rx` state only; no UI layout in controllers.

## New screen checklist

1. Add string keys to `app_strings.dart` + `locales/en_us.dart`.
2. Wire widget labels/buttons with `.tr`.
3. Move any new magic values to the right file under `utils/constants/`.
